{"author":{"id":"6d85cf2fcebaeefd8c5c528f2d5f5f98f26ce3275422d0dc5f7c0fd596f9f59f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791580796,"nonce":"D0CI0RJDEAp4absxlIc8emEZ5/w=","message":"Step 2 landed in 07317e1: css::cascade. A Cascade holds sheets in order, one atom table (each sheet keeps its own atoms and a map into it), the media environment, the theme's variables and the root font size. The host describes its tree through the Tree trait (parent, children, and per element its types, id, classes, attributes, inline declarations, state bits and whether it is anonymous) and styles parents first. Per element it returns Computed (values, inherited ones and custom properties included; resolved declarations with var() replaced; font-size in pixels) and Dependencies (which states of which nodes a selector tested, and whether the theme answered a var()), so the host knows when to style it again. Rules are found through an index keyed by the subject's id, first class or type.\n\nSemantics match the existing implementation: importance, then specificity, then sheet, rule and declaration order; inline over all but important; shorthands reset their longhands; inherited properties and custom properties pass down, inherited font properties applying to text elements alone; var() reads the element's values, then the sheets' :root variables, then the theme, ten levels deep at most.\n\nParity: a page of built-in elements and components (114 nodes: the user-agent sheet and the components library, 125 theme variables, dark scheme, with hover, focus, focus-visible, focus-within, checked, disabled and form states set) gives the same computed values for every element from the existing cascade and from this one. Seven unit tests cover order and importance, sheet order and removal, shorthands, inheritance and var(), combinators and structural pseudo-classes with :has, states and attributes with their dependencies, and media queries.\n\nNext: the cascade on LayoutContext (its atom table shared with the host's names, element data per node, restyling what changed), and applying values through layout_props, with the value readers ported.","files":null}]}